Day 8 — GCP Pub/Sub + Cloud Run + Event-Driven Architectures

Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ You need asynchronous communication between microservices with retry & dead-letter handling. How will you architect this using Pub/Sub?

2️⃣ A service experiences sudden traffic spikes and must scale to zero when idle. Which service will you use and how will you configure it?

3️⃣ Messages are being published faster than subscribers can process them. What optimizations will you apply (pull, push, batching, concurrency)?

4️⃣ You need event-driven automation each time a file lands in Cloud Storage. How will you design this end-to-end?

5️⃣ A real-time order processing system must not lose messages, even if consumer goes down. How will you design ack deadlines, retries and DLQs?

6️⃣ Cloud Run container cold starts are causing latency. What tuning strategies will you implement to reduce startup delays?

7️⃣ Your Pub/Sub consumer runs business logic + DB write operations. How will you ensure idempotency to avoid duplicate inserts?

8️⃣ A Cloud Run service must connect securely to VMs in a private VPC. How will you configure egress + VPC connectors + private routing?

9️⃣ You need multi-tenant message separation inside Pub/Sub. Will you isolate using topics, subscriptions, attributes, or separate projects? Explain.

🔟 Pub/Sub latency is high for large message loads. What performance tuning and architecture reviews would you do?

1️⃣1️⃣ You must build an ETL pipeline triggered by Pub/Sub and store results in BigQuery. How will you design batching + cost optimization?

1️⃣2️⃣ Sensitive events should not leave GCP network boundary. How will you combine Pub/Sub + VPC-SC + IAM?

1️⃣3️⃣ You need to schedule periodic workloads without running servers. Which GCP services fit best and how will you integrate them?

1️⃣4️⃣ A Cloud Run deployment broke production. How will you roll back quickly, enable traffic splitting and add safe release patterns?

1️⃣5️⃣ You must stream data from Pub/Sub to BigQuery with real-time transformations. When will you choose Dataflow over Cloud Functions?
